    pr_ref:  # 8d86
    description: "The WI-dajul concept vocabulary registry (docs/CONCEPTS.md, PR #3136) revealed 310 inert concepts — concepts that YAML patterns emit onto symbols but no linker consumes. Per INV-nimuj, linker priorities should follow expected false-positive-reduction volume, not novelty. The inert-concept tally is a direct proxy for that volume: how many frameworks produce the concept indicates how many symbol-dispatch gaps exist across the corpus.\n\nTop inert concepts by producer count (scanned 2026-04-18):\n\n| Concept | Producer count | Sample frameworks |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| error_handler | 37 | fastapi, express, django, aspnet, flask, actix, axum, gin, nestjs, ... |\n| controller | 34 | aspnet, rails, laravel, symfony, django, spring-mvc, yii, cakephp, ... |\n| websocket_handler | 21 | express, fastapi, nestjs, aspnet, django, phoenix, actix, ... |\n| event_handler | 17 | django, celery, rails, symfony, laminas, play, phoenix, ... |\n| application | 17 | aiohttp, tornado, giraffe, http4s, javalin, scotty, yesod, ... |\n| router | 14 | express, fastify, koa, hapi, nestjs, fastapi, sinatra, ... |\n| auth | 14 | adonisjs, akka-http, fastapi, flask, giraffe, grape, graphql, ktor, ... |\n| form | 12 | rails, django, laravel, symfony, aspnet, laminas, yii, ... |\n| task | 10 | celery, airflow, luigi, rq, dramatiq, sidekiq, ... |\n| response | 10 | express, fastapi, hapi, nestjs, aspnet, symfony, ... |\n| component | 10 | react, vue, angular, svelte, solid, preact, mithril, ... |\n\nScope of this item\n\nBuild a single Protocol-subcategory linker that maps error_handler / controller concepts to their downstream wiring. Both are high producer-count AND have clean dispatch semantics (error_handler → framework error pipeline; controller → route-group registration). Do NOT try to cover all 10+ top inerts in one linker — pick the one with the clearest semantics (error_handler is recommended: every framework wires it via a small set of registration APIs).\n\nSuggested decomposition if we want multiple linkers:\n- Protocol linker: error_handler → HTTP error-response registration\n- Framework linker: controller → route-group containment (distinct from route_handler.py which already handles individual routes)\n- Protocol linker: event_handler → message-dispatch target (overlaps with message_dispatch.py; verify before building)\n\nAcceptance\n\nPick one inert concept from the table above. Build a linker that emits meaningful edges on at least 3 bakeoff-cohort repositories (not just a single framework's fixture). Update docs/CONCEPTS.md via scripts/generate-concepts — the newly-consumed concept should flip from `inert` to `live` automatically.\n\nThis item is the umbrella; split into one concrete linker item once the target concept is chosen. Do not attempt without re-reviewing INV-nimuj and the per-linker scope of ADR-0003-ext."  # 8d86
    fields: {}  # 8d86
