  message: "Phase 3 shipped: router-concept containment linker merged in PR #3193 (commit 00ffb9014 on dev). Emits `registers_routes` edges from `concept: router` module/combinator/route-table symbols to nested `concept: route` registrations. Edge type distinct from controller_routes' `contains_routes` (controllers contain handler methods; routers contain registration call sites). Flipped `router` inert → live in docs/CONCEPTS.md (14 producer frameworks). 18 new tests, 100% coverage, per-package isolation validated. Remaining inert concepts by producer count for future phases: auth=14, form=12, response=10, component=10, validator=9, server=9, serializer=9, service=8, route_group=8, request=8, handler=8, config=8."  # 6864
- op: discuss  # 710c
  at: '2026-04-19T12:34:00Z'  # 710c
  by: agent  # 710c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 710c
  clock: 6  # 710c
  nonce: 710c  # 710c
  message: "Phase 4 scoping note (for next session):\n\nPost-Phase-3 remaining top inerts by producer count:\n- auth (14): NON-uniform semantics — some frameworks mark auth middleware, some mark auth handler routes, some mark policies/roles. A single entrypoint mapping would be noisy. Needs per-producer analysis before scope decision.\n- form (12, rails/django/laravel/symfony/aspnet/...): class-level concept where framework calls form.is_valid() / save() / authorize() reflectively. Clean candidate for ENTRYPOINT classification (class as entrypoint at confidence ~0.85) OR dispatches_to on known form-base method sets (django_orm_dispatch template). Entrypoint-only recovers class reachability but not internal method reachability; full dispatch requires per-framework method name registry.\n- response (10): likely not an entrypoint or container — response is typically a return-value marker, not a dispatchable class. May be a pure tagging concept with no dispatch edges to emit. Audit before adding linker.\n- component (10, react/vue/angular/svelte/solid/preact/mithril/lit/phoenix/spring-boot): components contain lifecycle methods (render/componentDidMount/setup/onMount/ngOnInit). Method names are framework-specific — needs name-based dispatch registry like airflow_framework_dispatch or django_orm_dispatch. NOT a simple concept-containment match because lifecycle methods aren't tagged with concepts. react_component.py already handles JSX composition, not this.\n- validator (9), server (9), serializer (9): likely all dispatch-style linkers requiring per-framework method registries.\n\n**Recommended Phase 4 pick:** form. Rationale: (a) highest-producer after the ambiguous-semantics ones, (b) entrypoint classification alone (class as entrypoint) is a defensible minimum with clean scope, (c) method-dispatch extension can be a Phase 4b follow-up. Acceptance: detect_entrypoints maps concept:form → EntrypointKind.FORM (or reuse existing Class entrypoint with FORM label), confidence 0.85, framework-aware label, per-symbol dedup, docs/CONCEPTS.md flips inert → live, 100% coverage.\n\nDeferred until a future session picks this up."  # 710c
