- op: discuss  # f02a
  at: '2026-04-19T14:09:20Z'  # f02a
  by: agent  # f02a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f02a
  clock: 8  # f02a
  nonce: f02a  # f02a
  message: "Validator concept (9 producers) semantics audit — DEFERRED from Phase 5 pickup:\n\nUnlike form (uniformly class-level across all 12 producers), validator has heterogeneous semantics:\n- adonisjs: base_class BaseValidator (class-level ✅)\n- hanami: base_class Hanami::Validations / Dry::Validation::Contract (class-level ✅)\n- laminas: interface-based (class-level ✅)\n- aspnet: annotation-based (Required, StringLength, Range, etc.) on MODEL FIELDS — these aren't dispatchable classes, they're field metadata\n- hapi: decorator-based (Joi.object / Joi.string calls) on SCHEMA DEFINITIONS — these aren't dispatchable either; they're data-shape declarations\n- masonite / rails: mixed — sometimes classes, sometimes validation method declarations\n- yii / symfony: class-level\n\nMapping validator → entrypoint would over-trigger: aspnet field annotations and hapi Joi schema declarations would become bogus entrypoints even though they're not called reflectively — they're consumed by the framework's validator runtime as data, not as handlers.\n\nRecommendation: split validator into per-producer analysis before unifying. Class-level producers (adonisjs, hanami, laminas, yii, symfony, masonite) could map to a new CLASS_VALIDATOR entrypoint kind at confidence 0.80; annotation-level (aspnet) and decorator-call-level (hapi) producers need separate linkers (annotation-validator → DUMMY_USE edge; decorator-call validator → already covered by decorator_dispatch). Not worth a single-PR simplification.\n\nCleaner Phase 5 candidates to consider instead:\n- server (9 producers, http4s / scotty / vertx / cowboy / http4k / servant / pedestal / plumber / shiny): likely all server-bootstrap entrypoints (MAIN_FUNCTION-style). Relatively uniform.\n- task (10, celery / airflow / luigi / rq / dramatiq / sidekiq / ...): already mapped via background_task concept in Phase 0; double-check why 'task' stays inert.\n- mailer (7, cakephp / fuelphp / hanami / laminas / laravel / padrino / rails): class-level, frameworks invoke deliver/send reflectively. Clean entrypoint candidate.\n\nStopping WI-gudob chain here for this session — 3 phases in one day (controller+router+form, 31 inert→live flips) is meaningful progress and diminishing returns kick in below 10 producers per concept."  # f02a
